    "library": "One distinct (group, artifact, version). Undeclared jars identified by manifest or hash.",
    "loc": "Lines of code per file split into code, comment and blank using the language's comment syntax. A line holding both code and a comment counts as code. Every text file is counted under the language its extension names; a text extension no rule knows is listed as 'other (.ext)'. Binary files (by extension, a NUL byte or mostly control bytes, e.g. .class, .o, .exe) are left out, data files (.dat, .csv) and backup copies (.bak, .old, ~, .java_old, .sql.20190312) are listed with no lines.",
    "screen": "One rendered UI page or map: JSP/JSF/HTML page that is a forward/view target, BMS map, terminal form. JSP fragments/tiles are counted separately as partials.",
